==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|non|gem-pro|*hlaupaną}}, whence also Old English {{m|ang|hlēapan}} ( > English {{term|leap|lang=en}}), Old Frisian {{term|hlapa|lang=ofs}} ( > West Frisian {{m|fy|ljeppe}}), Old Saxon {{m|osx|hlōpan}} ( > Low German {{m|nds|lopen}}),  Dutch {{term|lopen|lang=nl}}, Old High German {{term|hlaufan|lang=goh}} ( > German {{term|laufen|lang=de}}). Ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|non}} {{m|ine-pro|*klAub-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*klAup-||to spring, stumble}}.

===Verb===
{{non-verb|hljóp|hljópu|hlaupinn}}

# to [[leap]], [[jump]], [[spring]]

